0..75 Comment "// A rule a theory\'s completion derives, stated as a declaration of its own"
76..147 Comment "// and proved for every model: `derive r : l <=> r in T` holds when the"
148..222 Comment "// theory\'s completed rules rewrite both sides to one normal form, and the"
223..299 Comment "// rewrites are the proof. The group\'s laws derive the inverse of a product:"
300..378 Comment "// each rule completion derived on the way is proved first, from the two paths"
379..455 Comment "// of its certificate, then the statement from both sides\' rewrites to their"
456..531 Comment "// common normal form (Knuth and Bendix, _Simple Word Problems in Universal"
532..609 Comment "// Algebras_, 1970, § 7). The rule is read at a model as the theory\'s member"
610..628 Comment "// `Group.invMul`."
630..682 Comment "// The group\'s unit, associativity and inverse laws."
